    "detailed_description": "It's winter break 1994 and schools out at <i>Harthorn High School</i>, but not all is silent in its empty classrooms and dark hallways...<br><br>In a sudden change: Harthorn has upgraded its security, including new locks, alarmed windows, and <i>you</i> patrolling it's halls as the new part-time security guard. One night aided by your radio dispatcher, <i>April</i>, you investigate a broken window not into the school, but out of it, which leads to a story-driven dive into psychological horror.  <br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Explore the vast Harthorn, every room can be entered in a true-to-life high school.<br></li><li>Talking to April, solving puzzles, reading notes, and checking your map are keys to survival.<br></li><li>You're not alone: carelessness is repaid with lethal consequences.</li></ul><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1397110/extras/c7cc1ea10eb256b6c633deefdbcad839.avif?t=1679147845\" /></div><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">The Gameplay:</h2><br><strong>Immersive Horror:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Harthorn is story driven and fully narrated by talented voice actors.<br></li><li>Detailed environments beckon exploration, from gymnasiums to frozen forests.<br></li><li>Find clues that tell a bigger story, the more you investigate the more you'll learn.<br></li><li>Discover the true terror of Harthorn and whose behind (or under) it.<br><br><strong>Genre:</strong> Harthorn is a short story driven <i>psychological horror</i> game with dialog, puzzles, and exploration at its core.<br><br><i>From the creator of:</i><br><br><br><br></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "It's winter break 1994 and schools out at <i>Harthorn High School</i>, but not all is silent in its empty classrooms and dark hallways...<br><br>In a sudden change: Harthorn has upgraded its security, including new locks, alarmed windows, and <i>you</i> patrolling it's halls as the new part-time security guard. One night aided by your radio dispatcher, <i>April</i>, you investigate a broken window not into the school, but out of it, which leads to a story-driven dive into psychological horror.  <br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Explore the vast Harthorn, every room can be entered in a true-to-life high school.<br></li><li>Talking to April, solving puzzles, reading notes, and checking your map are keys to survival.<br></li><li>You're not alone: carelessness is repaid with lethal consequences.</li></ul><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1397110/extras/c7cc1ea10eb256b6c633deefdbcad839.avif?t=1679147845\" /></div><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">The Gameplay:</h2><br><strong>Immersive Horror:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Harthorn is story driven and fully narrated by talented voice actors.<br></li><li>Detailed environments beckon exploration, from gymnasiums to frozen forests.<br></li><li>Find clues that tell a bigger story, the more you investigate the more you'll learn.<br></li><li>Discover the true terror of Harthorn and whose behind (or under) it.<br><br><strong>Genre:</strong> Harthorn is a short story driven <i>psychological horror</i> game with dialog, puzzles, and exploration at its core.<br><br><i>From the creator of:</i><br><br><br><br></li></ul>",
